1
00:00:00,960 --> 00:00:06,280
Matthew 20 For the kingdom of heaven is like a master

2
00:00:06,280 --> 00:00:10,240
of a house who went out early in the morning to hire laborers for his vineyard.

3
00:00:10,920 --> 00:00:15,920
After agreeing with the laborers for a denarius a day, he sent them into his vineyard.

4
00:00:16,480 --> 00:00:20,540
And going out about the third hour he saw others standing idle in the marketplace.

5
00:00:21,420 --> 00:00:26,400
And to them he said, You go into the vineyard too, and whatever is right I will give you.

6
00:00:26,400 --> 00:00:33,160
20 So they went, going out again about the sixth hour, and the ninth hour he did the same.

7
00:00:33,840 --> 00:00:38,660
And about the eleventh hour he went out and found others standing, and he said to them,

8
00:00:38,940 --> 00:00:44,620
Why do you stand here idle all day? They said to him, Because no one has hired us.

9
00:00:45,240 --> 00:00:51,060
He said to them, You go into the vineyard too. And when evening came, the owner of the vineyard

10
00:00:51,060 --> 00:00:56,340
said to his foreman, Call the laborers and pay them their wages, beginning with the last,

11
00:00:56,560 --> 00:01:02,240
up to the first. And when those hired about the eleventh hour came, each of them received a

12
00:01:02,240 --> 00:01:08,560
denarius. Now when those hired first came, they thought they would receive more, but each of them

13
00:01:08,560 --> 00:01:14,820
also received a denarius. And on receiving it they grumbled at the master of the house, saying,

14
00:01:15,180 --> 00:01:21,460
These last work only one hour, and you have made them equal to us, who have borne the burden of

15
00:01:21,460 --> 00:01:25,360
the day and the scorching heat. But he replied to one of them,

16
00:01:25,880 --> 00:01:26,380
Friend,

17
00:01:26,560 --> 00:01:31,040
I am doing you no wrong. Did you not agree with me for a denarius?

18
00:01:31,820 --> 00:01:38,680
Take what belongs to you and go. I choose to give to this last worker as I give to you.

19
00:01:39,300 --> 00:01:43,040
Am I not allowed to do what I choose with what belongs to me?

20
00:01:43,960 --> 00:01:50,840
Or do you begrudge my generosity? So the last will be first, and the first last.

21
00:01:51,360 --> 00:01:55,940
And as Jesus was going up to Jerusalem, he took the twelve disciples aside,

22
00:01:55,940 --> 00:01:56,380
and he said to them, I am doing you no wrong. Did you not agree with me for a denarius?

23
00:01:56,380 --> 00:02:00,760
And on the way he said to them, See, we are going up to Jerusalem,

24
00:02:01,180 --> 00:02:06,300
and the Son of Man will be delivered over to the chief priests and scribes, and they will condemn

25
00:02:06,300 --> 00:02:13,180
him to death, and deliver him over to the Gentiles to be mocked and flogged and crucified. And he

26
00:02:13,180 --> 00:02:19,380
will be raised on the third day. Then the mother of the sons of Zebedee came up to him with her

27
00:02:19,380 --> 00:02:26,000
sons, and kneeling before him she asked him for something. And he said to her, What do you want?

28
00:02:26,380 --> 00:02:32,100
She said to him, Say that these two sons of mine are to sit,

29
00:02:32,520 --> 00:02:36,680
one at your right hand and one at your left, in your kingdom.

30
00:02:37,500 --> 00:02:44,140
Jesus answered, You do not know what you are asking. Are you able to drink the cup that I am

31
00:02:44,140 --> 00:02:52,380
to drink? They said to him, We are able. He said to them, You will drink my cup,

32
00:02:52,380 --> 00:02:56,360
but to sit at my right hand and at my left is not mine to drink.

33
00:02:56,380 --> 00:03:00,360
But it is for those for whom it has been prepared by my Father.

34
00:03:01,160 --> 00:03:04,260
And when the ten heard it they were indignant at the two brothers.

35
00:03:04,940 --> 00:03:11,420
But Jesus called them to him and said, You know that the rulers of the Gentiles lord it over them,

36
00:03:11,740 --> 00:03:17,100
and their great ones exercise authority over them. It shall not be so among you,

37
00:03:17,580 --> 00:03:23,000
but whoever would be great among you must be your servant, and whoever would be first among you

38
00:03:23,000 --> 00:03:26,360
must be your slave. Even as the Son of Man,

39
00:03:26,380 --> 00:03:32,460
came not to be served, but to serve, and to give his life as a ransom for many.

40
00:03:34,200 --> 00:03:40,100
And as they went out of Jericho, a great crowd followed him. And behold, there were two blind

41
00:03:40,100 --> 00:03:44,460
men sitting by the roadside, and when they heard that Jesus was passing by, they cried out,

42
00:03:45,020 --> 00:03:52,660
Lord, have mercy on us, son of David. The crowd rebuked them, telling them to be silent,

43
00:03:52,660 --> 00:03:55,940
but they cried out all the more, Lord,

44
00:03:56,380 --> 00:04:03,340
have mercy on us, son of David. And, stopping, Jesus called them and said,

45
00:04:04,220 --> 00:04:07,900
What do you want me to do for you? They said to him,

46
00:04:08,780 --> 00:04:16,300
Lord, let our eyes be opened. And Jesus in pity touched their eyes,

47
00:04:16,300 --> 00:04:19,820
and immediately they recovered their sight and followed him.

